    "pattern": "Data Structure Design",
    "summary": "Map each key to (value, uses); keep one doubly linked list per use count, oldest first, and track the fewest uses. A use moves a key up one list; eviction takes the oldest key of the fewest-uses list.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) per call",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(capacity)",
    "whenToUse": [
      "A cache that evicts the least frequently used entry, oldest first on ties",
      "Counts that only ever rise by one, so the minimum can be tracked directly"
    ]
